name 'aif-y2-ai-at-scale-postassessment-q2-2026'

wrong 'The company could sort apples more quickly, and they\'ll make fewer mistakes.'
wrong 'The company could sort apples more quickly, but they\'ll make more mistakes.'
right 'The company could sort apples more quickly, and they\'ll make the same number of mistakes.'
wrong 'The company could sort apples less quickly, but they\'ll make fewer mistakes.'

allow_multiple_attempts true

markdown <<MARKDOWN
A produce company harvests apples. Afterward, they need to sort their harvest: that is, separate good apples from bad apples. The company is considering whether an AI system would be a worthwhile investment.

The company usually harvests 100,000 apples. A team of humans can sort 1,000 apples per day with 98% accuracy. The AI system could sort 10,000 apples per day with 98% accuracy.

Which best describes the expected results of the sorting process after adopting the AI system?
MARKDOWN

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
Lesson 1: Challenges at Scale
MARKDOWN
